WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
Some surprising

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.569
developments at the US-Mexico border.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.436
The number of migrant

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.371
crossings has dropped

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.739
significantly in the days

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.008
since Title 42 expired just last week.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.843
Border officials had seen record

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.910
numbers of migrants

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.945
trying to enter the US,

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.613
but in the last three days or so.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:14.381
Department of Homeland

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.181
Security officials

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.283
say they've seen a 50% drop

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.518
in migrant crossings.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.619
And joining us with more on

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.721
this is former Texas Governor Rick Perry,

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.823
who also served as energy secretary

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.725
during the Trump administration.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.826
Governor, great to see you.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.261
Really appreciate it.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.996
I know you had to deal with border issues

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:30.797
as well.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:31.831
When you were governor,

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:32.899
why do you think we're hearing

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.666
about these lower

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.569
than expected numbers so far?

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:37.370
Yeah.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.438
Before we start,

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.440
let's just wish every mother out there

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.608
happy Mother's Day

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.110
and what a great day to reflect

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:44.911
how blessed

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.147
we are to have some wonderful

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.515
women in this world. So

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.285
back to your question.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.721
And listen, taking a snapshot in time

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.323
is a snapshot in time.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.892
This issue has been going on.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.559
As a matter of fact,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.428
I was digging around in my office.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.929
I don't know if you see this or not.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.432
This is a Homeland Security Committee

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.033
briefing book

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:07.901
that I just happened

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:11.371
to see on my disheveled office in here.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.606
It's dated 2014.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.875
And we're dealing with the

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.278
field hearing crisis on the Texas border.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.513
Surge of unaccompanied minors.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.514
You remember that?

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.549
That was

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.684
nine years ago.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.052
So this has been going on

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.021
for a really long time.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.990
We've had now three administrations that

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:31.858
dealt with it.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:32.792
I'm very

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.494
biased in my observation

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.629
as I think we had

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.432
this issue in hand and four years ago

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.868
with the programs that we had in place,

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.002
the message was clear.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.805
It's not just a casual walk

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.340
across the border to get into

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.275
the United States. And so

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.144
I think you

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.446
have to go back to some really strict

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.150
enforcement of the of the border.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.986
You have to have a system in place

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:03.523
where you can allow for legal immigration

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:07.026
and you have to have these countries

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:10.063
south of the border working with you.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.298
And I think we may have failed

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.700
there more often

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:14.968
than we were successful

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.370
in getting these countries and central

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.307
and Mexico, Central America and Mexico.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.743
So there's a lot of work to be done.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.578
And we got a real problem on our hands.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.213
And we don't know who these people are.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.082
And that's the that's the real challenge.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:32.886
So but we need we need to come together

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.154
this this deal

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.822
and in a circle and pointing to the left

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.323
and saying it's their fault

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.491
we know how to do this.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.792
So let's,

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:40.560
you know,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.695
say and saying this is easier than it is

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:43.329
to get it done.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.330
I recognize that.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.798
But the Biden administration

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.333
needs to get serious about

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.735
what's going on on the border.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.469
Well, as you know,

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:50.570
your state has been in the news

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.472
a lot over the last few weeks.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.106
Just last week,

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:53.907
we saw that mass

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.909
shooting in Allen, Texas,

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.243
one of a rash of massacres

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.312
we've seen in Texas in recent years,

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.213
including the tragedy.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.081
And you've all these just last year

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:02.782
and last week,

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:03.783
I had to ask you about this

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.351
because you served as governor

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.419
of the state of Texas.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.420
A state House committee

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.689
voted to raise the minimum age,

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.225
I should say, from 18 to 21

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.061
to purchase an AR 15 style rifle.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.230
But that measure failed to advance.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.064
What do you think?

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.300
Do you support raising that purchase age

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.734
in Texas?

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.370
You and I are going to

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.471
talk about an issue

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.339
that really may have

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.607
a lot more to do with that

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.142
than raising the age

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:31.477
of whether someone can have a weapon.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.580
And that's this issue of mental health.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.747
And, you know,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:35.615
that is where

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.917
we need to be focusing a lot.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.018
We need to make sure

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.287
that our schools are secure

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.323
and that we have the security

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.490
around those schools.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.326
And that requires weapons.

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:47.961
And in the state of Texas,

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:50.463
we're going to keep the weapons.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.331
We're going to

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:54.167
you should be increasing the amount

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:54.701
of security

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.069
that we have around places

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.770
and people that we love.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.838
That's how you stop bad

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.540
people with weapons,

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.208
not by raising the minimum age of

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.744
when someone can buy a weapon

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.347
and let's talk about mental health.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:08.348
I know that

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:08.915
this is something

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.650
that you've been working on

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.819
when it comes to veterans.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:13.319
You know,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.520
this issue of mental health

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.755
has been an issue

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.723
in the veteran community

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.557
for some time now,

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.292
for several years, though.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.360
I wanted to ask you about this.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.361
You've been an outspoken

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.962
proponent for the legalization

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:25.865
of psychedelic drugs for therapeutic use.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:26.966
We're talking about things

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.101
like magic mushrooms,

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.303
as they're commonly called.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.471
Tell me why a conservative

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.705
former Texas governor thinks

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:33.640
that's a good idea.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.075
Yeah.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:36.943
Ten years ago, if he

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.444
had said my name and psychedelics

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.612
are going to be in the same sentence,

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.813
I would've said you're crazy.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.015
But there are a lot of things

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.116
that have happened in my life

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:43.883
that have

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.019
really changed my mind about it.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.253
You know, I grew up in the sixties.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.889
I was a total and absolute against

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.724
legalization of drugs.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:52.825
And I still am

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.694
for the standpoint of recreational use

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:55.695
and what have you.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.929
But these compounds,

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.165
when they're used with the right dosage,

00:04:59.198 --> 00:04:59.899
well, obviously

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:00.266
the right

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.801
diagnosis, the first right

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:02.702
dosage, the right

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.904
and guiding through these

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.273
these experiences and the follow up,

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:09.042
those four things together.

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:09.842
And we're seeing some

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.544
extraordinary benefits from

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.079
let me just give you one example up

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:14.647
in New York. In the VA,

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.049
there's a

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.383
doctor, Rachel Yehuda,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.152
who is overseeing a program there.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.720
I think they have two phase

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.322
three trials behind them now

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:25.658
using MDMA the old rave drug ecstasy.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.662
And the the the benefits of that

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.831
and the results of those trials

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.032
are stunningly good.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:33.633
For instance,

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:36.002
and I'll try to be brief here

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:39.539
they are three doses two weeks apart

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.341
to these veterans

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.842
who had post-traumatic stress

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:43.743
symptoms either

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.977
depression, anxiety,

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.612
sleeplessness, suicidal thoughts,

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:49.115
or are all four in a lot of cases.

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:53.553
After six months, after three doses

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:56.689
70 plus percent of those individuals

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:57.857
had zero

00:05:57.857 --> 00:06:00.660
symptoms of post-traumatic stress.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.395
Jim, I don't know.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:06.232
You know, to me that is stunning results.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.634
It's one that we as a country

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:09.635
need to get behind.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.671
It's my understanding that the FDA

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.473
is going to approve

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.742
or taken off of schedule one

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:17.343
MDMA in the fall.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.145
I think that is very wise.

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.813
I think the VA

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:21.614
is supporting

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:23.282
that and all Americans should

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:25.685
if you care about these kids lives,

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:26.619
young men and women

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.021
who put their lives on the line for us.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.223
We were at war for 20

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:31.691
years, was a whole nother story.

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:34.627
But for 20 years, they've been in combat

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.629
and to be able to

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.164
give them their lives back

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:38.765
after they

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:40.833
literally put their lives on the line.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.469
And sadly, somewhere between 16 and 20

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.906
are still committing suicide every day.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.542
Yeah, we need to get serious about this.

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.711
We've got some compounds

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:52.512
that we're seeing.

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:53.613
Great results with,

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:54.714
and I think that

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:56.215
Americans all across the board

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.351
should educate yourself about it.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.552
I told you offline

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.788
that this is kind of like nuclear power

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:04.590
that, you know, in the sixties

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.392
